driver was calculated at 1,132 feet, as measured from the area of impact (AASHTO 2011). 50 Based
on the [car manufacturer]’s 74-mph approach speed and the calculated line-of-sight distance, both drivers could
potentially have had up to 10.4 seconds to observe and respond to one another. 51

