vehicles, AASHTO guidelines recommend intersection sight distances of 781 and 842 feet for
highway design speeds of 65 and 70 mph, respectively. Those distances are based on a minimum
gap time of 8.2 seconds (7.5 seconds for a combination vehicle plus 0.7 second for crossing the
additional through lane). 52 Therefore, the calculated sight distance of 1,132 feet for the truck driver
exceeded the minimum sight distance that AASHTO recommends for a roadway of this design
